Author: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date:   Tue Nov 24 18:34:10 2026 +0000

    Store: a failed completePurchase no longer aborts the purchase batch
    
    Found by the StoreKit Test E2E run 45454802455 (iOS 26.2 simulator): the
    first StoreKit Test transaction has id 0, which in_app_purchase_storekit
    0.4.17 cannot finish (null-check error in completePurchase). The exception
    escaped _onPurchases, so later transactions in the batch were not handled
    and listeners were not notified. Finishing errors are now logged and
    contained; the entitlement still comes from StoreKit's current entitlements.
    Unit test added (fails without the fix).
    
    Reuse check: existing AppStoreService and its scripted-IAP tests.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
    Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01UBUdYmsJtDfAqW8QfATVTw

